Description: ARM: dts: imx: add the i.MX21 and the Chumby Classic
 imx21.dtsi follows imx27.dtsi with the i.MX21's memory map, interrupts,
 clocks and DMA requests. The SSIs name their DMA channels "rx" and
 "tx", as the dmaengine PCM looks them up.
 .
 The Chumby Classic (hardware 3.8) translates its former board file: the
 panel, the keypad port as GPIO (button, LCD power, speaker shutdown,
 Wi-Fi power), the TSC2100 on CSPI3, the accelerometer on CSPI1, the PWM
 backlight and three USB host ports. Its boot loader passes ATAGs, so
 the DTB is appended to the zImage. UART2 is enabled though nothing on
 the board is wired to it, without pins: an emulated Chumby, which has no
 network, reaches neochumbyd over it (ttymxc1).
Author: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AI generated code]
Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Ee1gRFAS7tp8oLbvQ
---
